sign tonight Halloween a very dangerous  time for our pets chocolate toxic to  both dogs and cats but that is not the  only threat a look now at Halloween  hazards and the symptoms you need to  look out for if you think your pet has  gotten into those treats  every Halloween trick-or-treaters return  home with all sorts of goodies great for  the kiddos but you should never share  these treats with your pets not all  candy is the same it has a lot to do  with is it chocolate or not chocolate  what else is in it there are several  Halloween hazards pet parents should be  most concerned about the first chocolate  it contains ingredients that dogs are  much more sensitive to than people white  chocolate not as toxic as milk chocolate  dark or semi-sweet chocolate but no  amount is safe and if your dog displays  the following behaviors contact Animal  Poison Control signs of chocolate  toxicity would be things like  hyperactivity muscle Tremors and  elevated heart rate gastrointestinal  upset vomiting and diarrhea and in  extreme cases they can even have  seizures candy corn and other  ingredients in candy such as high  amounts of sugar and fat can cause  severe stomach upset for dogs and it too  can be fatal grapes raisins and  raisinets also a problem it only takes  us small amount to poison your pet these  items can cause kidney failure in dogs  candy wrappers can cause serious  problems as well with intestinal  obstructions dogs can sniff out all  these sweet treats so place them into a  cabinet they can't get into or an  airtight container and if you have any  concerns if your dog has eaten any  amount of Halloween candy call your  veterinarian or call animal poison  control  another thing to note keeps sugar-free  gum away from your pets it contains the  artificial sweetener Xylitol which is  also toxic to dogs
 

